{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS159dTcYGqBoVbA41a4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job was running all along. `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`. Two bugs stacked, and together they hid the failure. I couldn't run launchd, `claude` or Telegram here, so none of this is tested.\n\n**Causes**\n1. **Login failure:** the `.err` log says \"Not logged in · Please run /login\" on every run. The plist has no `USER` in `EnvironmentVariables`, so under launchd `claude` can't reach its login in the keychain.\n2. **Silent failure reporter:** the same log shows `nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status`. In zsh `status` is read-only, so `status=$?` killed the script before it could send the failure notification.\n\n**Changes**\n- **Plist:** added `USER=vk`.\n- **Script, the fix:** `status=$?` is now `rc=$?`.\n- **Script, extras:**\n  - `claude` now gets `< /dev/null` as stdin.\n  - The run duration is logged and included in the notification.\n  - An empty output file now sends a failure notice, so exit 0 with nothing done can't pass silently.\n\n**Colleague's note:** most of it applied. I used `< /dev/null` instead of piping the prompt through stdin, since your prompt reaches `claude` fine as an argument. `ANSWER.md` has the full list.\n\nTo check it on your machine:\n1. Copy the files into your home dir.\n2. Reload the job with `launchctl bootout`, then `launchctl bootstrap`, then `launchctl kickstart -k`. The exact commands are in `ANSWER.md`.\n3. Confirm exit code 0, a fresh non-empty output file, a plausible duration and a Telegram message.\n4. Force one failure to check the failure path.\n\nIf \"Not logged in\" persists, run `claude /login` once in a normal terminal. `notify.sh` also reads the keychain, so check that it works under launchd too."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cac